NAME-COLLISION RESOLUTION (binding decision recorded for the audit trail)
  The flat native dir apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/ already holds the CHARGING-CURVE LoadingSkeleton.*
  shipped by P4 · 0088 (web features/charging/components/charging-curve/LoadingSkeleton.tsx — committed
  8fef69845, log p4-apple-feature-views-0088-LoadingSkeleton.log present, STATUS=DONE). Both P-0088 and this
  P-0115 declare the identical "Native output / Allowed files = LoadingSkeleton.*" — a prompt-generator
  collision keyed on the shared basename. The two web sources are STRUCTURALLY DIFFERENT surfaces
  (charging-curve: 7 regions, filters, summary/comparison/footer stat grids, no table, no FadeIn; cost-analysis:
  4 regions, header action button, 3-block cards, a 5-row table, fractional widths, FadeIn wrapper).
  Resolution (preserves 0088, honours covenant pts 2/7/9, stays inside the allowed glob):
    • ship under LoadingSkeleton.CostAnalysis.* — every name matches the shell glob `LoadingSkeleton.*`
      (literal dot after "LoadingSkeleton"), so it is inside the prompt's Allowed-files scope;
    • use distinct Swift symbols (CostAnalysisLoadingSkeleton* / CA*) so both surfaces coexist in the one
      TeslaSync module with zero symbol clash (verified: 0 pre-existing definitions of any new symbol);
    • the 0088 charging-curve files are NOT touched (no predecessor bypass / no regression).
  The P1/S11 view.opened slug stays the prompt-specified literal "LoadingSkeleton" (both prompts mandate it);
  the surface is disambiguated at the file + type level, not the slug.

